WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.868
[MUSIC PLAYING]

00:00:06.220 --> 00:00:08.620
NARRATOR: Septic tanks are
the perfect sewage treatment

00:00:08.620 --> 00:00:11.545
solution for houses that aren't
connected to a sewage network.

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:16.630
The tank collects and
treats domestic wastewater

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:20.080
using a bacterial process
to decompose waste.

00:00:20.080 --> 00:00:22.600
It filters the dirty
water before recycling

00:00:22.600 --> 00:00:23.575
it back into the ground.

00:00:28.200 --> 00:00:30.750
Septic tanks are
usually made of concrete

00:00:30.750 --> 00:00:32.549
and have access covers on top.

00:00:34.110 --> 00:00:36.120
The waste treatment
process takes place

00:00:36.120 --> 00:00:38.220
in separate chambers
inside the tank.

00:00:43.100 --> 00:00:45.800
Steel bars called
rebars reinforce the

00:00:45.800 --> 00:00:47.450
concrete structure of the tank.

00:00:50.230 --> 00:00:53.500
A welder assembles the
rods to form a cage,

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:56.545
then he spot welds the rebar
with a mid welding torch.

00:01:00.430 --> 00:01:03.400
The welded cage will maintain
the structural integrity

00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:04.870
of the concrete septic tank.

00:01:08.330 --> 00:01:10.850
The welder measures
the cage's diagonals

00:01:10.850 --> 00:01:12.170
to make sure it's straight.

00:01:14.320 --> 00:01:16.690
Next, the worker
places rebar spacers

00:01:16.690 --> 00:01:20.010
to keep the cage centered in the
mold and leveled on the floor.

00:01:25.060 --> 00:01:28.570
A crane lowers the cage
into a custom formwork made

00:01:28.570 --> 00:01:29.980
of high strength steel plates.

00:01:32.400 --> 00:01:34.800
Workers close the
walls around the form

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:37.200
and secure them in place
with heavy duty locks.

00:01:40.350 --> 00:01:42.930
The crane lowers
machined steel cores

00:01:42.930 --> 00:01:45.300
to form the interior walls
of the tank chambers.

00:01:50.140 --> 00:01:54.010
A rigid plastic tube is
inserted inside a rubber sleeve

00:01:54.010 --> 00:01:55.960
to create a flow hole
between chambers.

00:01:58.170 --> 00:02:00.660
Using an acetylene
torch, a worker

00:02:00.660 --> 00:02:03.030
cuts holes in the rebar
for access openings.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:09.289
The mold allows concrete
to flow over the rebar

00:02:09.289 --> 00:02:12.500
and inbed the access opening
covers in the septic tank lid.

00:02:17.210 --> 00:02:21.370
Workers pour over 1,300 gallons
of wet concrete into the mold.

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:37.630
They use a stick vibrator
to eliminate air pockets

00:02:37.630 --> 00:02:39.640
and level the walls
with the putty knife.

00:02:43.300 --> 00:02:46.290
Next, they mix more
concrete and pour

00:02:46.290 --> 00:02:47.850
it over the top slab rebar.

00:02:50.850 --> 00:02:53.850
Concrete blocks are used to
keep the plastic covers from

00:02:53.850 --> 00:02:55.020
floating in the wet concrete.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:04.020
While one worker pours
the concrete in the mold,

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:06.930
the other consolidates the
mixture with a vibrating stick.

00:03:08.250 --> 00:03:11.325
Then a worker levels at the top
of the slab with the trowel.

00:03:15.230 --> 00:03:18.785
Once the concrete tank has
cured, workers strip the forms.

00:03:23.320 --> 00:03:26.620
They removed the concrete
tank using an overhead crane

00:03:26.620 --> 00:03:29.710
and a compressed air system,
which forces the mold away

00:03:29.710 --> 00:03:30.940
from the concrete tank.

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:38.365
The crane takes the strip
core away for cleanup.

00:03:46.250 --> 00:03:48.440
A worker brushes
the top of the walls

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:52.010
and sweeps the floor
inside the tank

00:03:52.010 --> 00:03:54.620
then he applies a butel
rubber tape around the top

00:03:54.620 --> 00:03:56.870
of the exterior wall.

00:03:56.870 --> 00:04:00.050
This forms a watertight seal
between the tank and the lid.

00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:06.110
An overhead crane lifts
the lid out of the formwork

00:04:06.110 --> 00:04:07.670
and brings it to the tank mold.

00:04:10.220 --> 00:04:13.580
The crane slowly lowers
the lid onto the tank.

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:16.325
Workers keep it align to
make sure it seals properly.

00:04:20.740 --> 00:04:23.530
Then they label the tank
to indicate its capacity.

00:04:26.680 --> 00:04:29.110
Next, the mold is
opened, revealing

00:04:29.110 --> 00:04:31.030
a finished septic tank.

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:33.250
The rubber sleeve
molded into the wall

00:04:33.250 --> 00:04:36.940
ensures a watertight connection
between the pipe carrying waste

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:38.740
from the home and the tank.

00:04:40.380 --> 00:04:42.500
This tank is now
ready for delivery.

00:04:46.710 --> 00:04:48.960
They set the tank in the
ground at the client's

00:04:48.960 --> 00:04:52.460
home using a radio remote
controlled knuckle boom crane.

00:04:56.360 --> 00:04:58.370
A septic tank like
this will provide

00:04:58.370 --> 00:05:00.560
a three bedroom
house with a fully

00:05:00.560 --> 00:05:01.880
independent sewage system.

00:05:01.880 --> 00:05:04.630
[MUSIC PLAYING]

